WEBVTT

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.920
Pause the video to figure it out yourself.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:02.713
Solution in 3

00:04:02.713 --> 00:04:03.633
Solution in 2

00:04:03.633 --> 00:04:04.713
Solution in 1

00:04:04.993 --> 00:04:08.034
Ethic’s conundrum seems sprawling 
on the surface,

00:04:08.034 --> 00:04:12.400
but there’s a remarkably simple
solution to it using recursion.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.150
In order to find it, let’s first look 
at the simplest version of this puzzle:

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.420
what if the entire maze 
were just two paths?

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:25.038
If Hedge copies himself, the copy 
that goes the wrong way will be destroyed.

00:04:25.038 --> 00:04:27.757
So the other one, 
which will reach the artifact,

00:04:27.757 --> 00:04:32.457
can radio back the path it took,
and then no matter which way is correct,